IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `isl-nouns`
IMPORT `isl-s01-definitions`
IMPORT `isl-p2-eligibility`
IMPORT `isl-sch1-young`
IMPORT `isl-p3-rates`
IMPORT `isl-p4-income`
IMPORT `isl-p5-claims-payment`
IMPORT `isl-p5-duties`
IMPORT `isl-p5-misc`

-- Income Support Law 5741-1980 (Israel), unofficial Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (revision 3073779) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Hebrew: חוק הבטחת הכנסה, התשמ״א–1980.
--
-- SEAT: a person or family living in Israel whose means fall short of the minimum the Law sets, asking whether they are entitled to an income-support
-- allowance, how much and from when, what they must do to keep it, what can reduce or stop it, and what they can be made to repay.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no
-- layer-1 module changed for it.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person
-- can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The records the modules expect (Household, Figures) are built inside each question,
-- in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here.
--
-- What a plain input hides, and where to look:
--   * The amounts the Law leaves to the National Insurance Institute and the Minister (the basic amount, the average wage, vehicle values, determining amounts)
--     are asked as numbers; the person finds them on the Institute's site.  The Law's own figures are the modules' constants.
--   * A judgment the Law leaves to an official or to the regulations (whether work is suitable, whether the regulations' conditions are met) is asked as a plain fact.
--   * An answer of NOTHING is "the Law does not cover this", not "no".  JUST FALSE is the Law's own "no".  See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".
--   * There is no question about a repayment of benefit as such: the Law has no section that says what a person must repay.  Ss 20A and 23(a) borrow the Insurance Law's
--     rules; the question under "What can I be made to repay?" says which of them applies, and the amount and the conditions are outside the sources.
--   * There is never a seat for an official.  Provisions that address only the Institute are encoded in layer 1 (s 13, s 21(a), s 25, s 26) and appear here only
--     for what they mean to the person.

§ `Income Support Law 5741-1980 -- the questions of a person or family living in Israel`

§§ `Am I entitled to the allowance? (ss 2 to 4)`

-- s 2(a)(1). A person who cannot work and support themselves, or cannot be placed in any work, is entitled -- if the Minister's rules are met and, for a
-- finding of non-placement, a named body made the finding for the situation the person is in.
@export Am I entitled because I cannot work or cannot be placed in any work (s 2(a)(1))?
GIVEN `I have no capacity to work and support myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established, under the rules of the Minister, that you have no capacity to work and to support yourself?
      `I cannot be placed in any work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it established, under the rules of the Minister, that you cannot be placed in any work?
      `my situation` IS A `Placement situation` @desc Which describes you: treated in an institution or in drug withdrawal under a court probation order; under a probation officer's supervision under the Arrests Law; staying at an alcoholics treatment centre under the Ministry's supervision; or none of these?
      `who found me not placeable` IS A Determiner @desc Who found that you cannot be placed in work: a drug-addiction diagnosis centre (or the institution treating you), a probation officer, an alcoholics treatment centre, or someone else?
      `the finding is for no longer than the Minister allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the finding for a period no longer than the Minister has set?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I cannot work or cannot be placed in any work` IS
    `s 2(a)(1) the person has no capacity to work or cannot be placed in any work`
        `I have no capacity to work and support myself`
        `I cannot be placed in any work`
        (`s 2(a)(1) the finding of non-placement was made by the body the text names for the situation` `my situation` `who found me not placeable`)
        `the finding is for no longer than the Minister allows`

-- s 2(a)(2). Registered as unemployed at the employment service under the rules for s 163 of the Insurance Law, and the service offered no suitable work.
@export Am I entitled because I am registered as unemployed and was offered no suitable work (s 2(a)(2))?
GIVEN `I am registered as unemployed at the employment service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you registered at the employment service as unemployed, under the rules fixed for s 163 of the National Insurance Law?
      `the employment service offered me suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the employment service offered you suitable work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I am registered as unemployed and was offered no suitable work` IS
    `s 2(a)(2) the person is registered as unemployed and was offered no suitable work`
        `I am registered as unemployed at the employment service`
        `the employment service offered me suitable work`

-- s 2(a)(3). Working, or in training, on an income below the income at which no benefit is paid, on the conditions the regulations set.
@export Am I entitled because I work or am in training on a low income (s 2(a)(3))?
GIVEN `I work or am in training or a rehabilitation framework` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work, or are you in training, including a rehabilitation framework supervised under the Law?
      `my income from the work or training` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly income from the work or training, in new shekels?
      `the income at which no allowance is paid` IS A NUMBER @desc At what monthly income is no allowance paid to someone in your family situation, in new shekels? (The Institute publishes it.)
      `I meet the conditions the regulations set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the conditions and tests that the regulations set for people who work or train?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I work or am in training on a low income` IS
    `s 2(a)(3) the person works or is in training with a low income`
        `I work or am in training or a rehabilitation framework`
        `my income from the work or training`
        `the income at which no allowance is paid`
        `I meet the conditions the regulations set`

-- s 2(a)(4). Retirement age.
@export Am I entitled because I have reached retirement age (s 2(a)(4))?
GIVEN `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age as the National Insurance Law defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I have reached retirement age` IS
    `s 2(a)(4) the person has reached retirement age` `I have reached retirement age`

-- s 2(a)(5). A parent of a child under two: the mother, unless the spouses chose that the other spouse be the one.
@export Am I entitled as a parent of a child under two (s 2(a)(5)(a))?
GIVEN `I am a parent of a child who is in my custody and with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child your child, in your custody and living with you?
      `my child's age in complete months` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is your child, in complete months?
      `the child's parents are spouses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the child's parents spouses?
      `I am the child's mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the child's mother?
      `we chose that the entitlement go to the parent who is not the mother` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the spouses choose that the entitlement go to the parent who is not the mother?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled as a parent of a child under two` IS
    `s 2(a)(5)(a) the parent of a child under two is entitled`
        `I am a parent of a child who is in my custody and with me`
        `my child's age in complete months`
        `the child's parents are spouses`
        `I am the child's mother`
        `we chose that the entitlement go to the parent who is not the mother`

-- s 2(a)(5)(b) and (c). Spouses who chose may change their choice: freely if the other spouse is not entitled under paragraph (2), otherwise every six months;
-- the change takes effect on the first of the next month after notice.
@export From when does a change of my choice take effect (s 2(a)(5)(c))?
GIVEN `the day I gave notice of the choice` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you give notice of your choice (or of its change)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From when does a change of my choice take effect` IS
    `s 2(a)(5)(c) the day the choice takes effect` `the day I gave notice of the choice`

@export May we change our choice of which parent is entitled (s 2(a)(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the other parent is entitled to the allowance as someone registered as unemployed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the parent who is not entitled as the parent of a child under two entitled under the registered-unemployed rule (s 2(a)(2))?
      `complete months since we last made or changed the choice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have gone by since you last made or changed the choice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we change our choice of which parent is entitled` IS
    `s 2(a)(5)(b) the spouses may change their choice`
        `the other parent is entitled to the allowance as someone registered as unemployed`
        `complete months since we last made or changed the choice`

-- s 2(a)(7). Main time goes to caring for a sick spouse or child who needs constant supervision.
@export Am I entitled because I mainly care for a sick spouse or child (s 2(a)(7))?
GIVEN `my main time goes to caring for a sick spouse or child who needs constant supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does most of your time go to caring for your sick spouse or child, who needs constant supervision?
      `I meet the rules the regulations set for such care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the rules, conditions and tests that the regulations set for this kind of care?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I mainly care for a sick spouse or child` IS
    `s 2(a)(7) the person's main time goes to caring for a sick spouse or child`
        `my main time goes to caring for a sick spouse or child who needs constant supervision`
        `I meet the rules the regulations set for such care`

-- s 2(a)(8). Community service under sub-chapter B1 of chapter 6 of the Penal Law.
@export Am I entitled because I am serving community service (s 2(a)(8))?
GIVEN `I am serving community service under the Penal Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you performing community service under sub-chapter B1 of chapter 6 of the Penal Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I am serving community service` IS
    `s 2(a)(8) the person performs community service` `I am serving community service under the Penal Law`

-- s 2(a)(9). A woman in a shelter for battered women, with the approval of the social services department or the Ministry, for more than 30 days.
@export Am I entitled because I am staying in a shelter for battered women (s 2(a)(9))?
GIVEN `I am a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman?
      `I am staying in an approved shelter for battered women` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you staying in a shelter for battered women with the approval of the social services department or the Ministry of Welfare?
      `the days I have stayed there` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have you stayed there?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I am staying in a shelter for battered women` IS
    `s 2(a)(9) the woman stays in a shelter for battered women`
        `I am a woman`
        `I am staying in an approved shelter for battered women`
        `the days I have stayed there`

-- s 2(a) and (b). A resident aged 25 or over is entitled if one ground of subsection (a) applies and, as a further condition, the person was a resident for
-- 24 consecutive months before the claim -- unless on a pension under chapter 5 or 11 of the Insurance Law.  The ground is the person's own summary of the questions above.
@export Am I entitled as a resident aged 25 or over (s 2(a) and (b))?
GIVEN `I am a resident of Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a resident of Israel?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `one of the grounds in s 2(a) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the grounds above (s 2(a)(1) to (5) and (7) to (9)) apply to you?
      `my complete consecutive months as a resident before I filed the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many complete consecutive months were you a resident of Israel before you filed your claim?
      `I receive a pension under chapter 5 or chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive a pension under chapter 5 (old age, disability and similar) or chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled as a resident aged 25 or over` IS
    `s 2(a) and (b) the resident aged 25 or over is entitled`
        (`s 2(a) the resident aged 25 or over is entitled under subsection (a)` `I am a resident of Israel` `my age in completed years` (LIST (`helper true or not covered` `one of the grounds in s 2(a) applies to me`)))
        (`s 2(b) the additional condition of 24 months of residence is met` `my complete consecutive months as a resident before I filed the claim` `I receive a pension under chapter 5 or chapter 11 of the National Insurance Law`)

-- s 2(e). A resident aged 20 to under 25 who would have been entitled had they been 25, and who proved they did all they could to enter work.
@export Am I entitled as a resident aged 20 to under 25 (s 2(e))?
GIVEN `I am a resident of Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a resident of Israel?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I would be entitled if I were 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled under s 2(a) and (b) if you were 25?
      `I proved that I did all I could to enter work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved, in the manner the Ministers fixed and to the satisfaction of the person they appointed, that you did all you could to enter work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled as a resident aged 20 to under 25` IS
    `s 2(e) the resident aged 20 to under 25 meets the two conditions`
        `I am a resident of Israel`
        `my age in completed years`
        (`helper true or not covered` `I would be entitled if I were 25`)
        `I proved that I did all I could to enter work`

-- s 2(d)(1) with First Schedule item 1(a). A child who is a resident and an orphan or abandoned child, aged under 20 and at school if 18 or over, not adopted into the
-- adopter's custody, and not kept at the expense of the State or a local authority.
@export Am I a child entitled as an orphan or abandoned child (s 2(d)(1), First Schedule item 1)?
GIVEN `I am a child who is a resident of Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a child (under 18, or 18 to 19 and finishing school) who is a resident of Israel?
      `I am an orphan or an abandoned child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an orphan, or a child abandoned in Israel by your parents (as item 1 of the First Schedule defines these)?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `my main time goes to finishing school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is most of your time devoted to finishing studies at a post-primary school?
      `I am an adopted child in the custody of my adopting parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopted child in the custody of the parent who adopted you?
      `the State or a local authority bears my upkeep` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State or a local authority bear your upkeep?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a child entitled as an orphan or abandoned child` IS
    `s 2(d)(1) the child who is a resident is entitled under item 1 of the First Schedule`
        `I am a child who is a resident of Israel`
        (`sch 1 item 1(a) the child meets the conditions` `I am an orphan or an abandoned child` `my age in completed years` `my main time goes to finishing school` `I am an adopted child in the custody of my adopting parent` `the State or a local authority bears my upkeep`)

-- s 2(d)(2) with First Schedule item 3. A resident under 25 who is a parent of a child in their custody.
@export Am I entitled as a parent under 25 of a child in my custody (s 2(d)(2), First Schedule item 3)?
GIVEN `I am a resident of Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a resident of Israel?
      `I am a parent of a child in my custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent of a child who is in your custody?
      `I would be entitled if I were 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled under s 2(a) and (b) if you were 25?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled as a parent under 25 of a child in my custody` IS
    `s 2(d)(2) the resident is entitled under an item of the First Schedule from item 2 onward`
        `I am a resident of Israel`
        (`sch 1 item 3 the person is a parent of a child in their custody` `I am a parent of a child in my custody`)
        (`helper true or not covered` `I would be entitled if I were 25`)

-- s 2(a)(2A) and s 2(d)(2) with First Schedule item 7. A pregnant woman aged 18 or over, in or after the 13th week.  Item 7 is on the list of s 2(a)(2A), which entitles a resident
-- "even if not yet 25" with no further test; s 2(d)(2) reaches it too but adds "had they been 25 they would have been entitled".  Either route is enough, and for item 7 the last input
-- never changes the answer (a yes under (2A) stands; where item 7 does not hold, neither route says yes).  It is kept so the question's inputs do not change.
@export Am I entitled because I am pregnant (s 2(a)(2A) and s 2(d)(2), First Schedule item 7)?
GIVEN `I am a resident of Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a resident of Israel?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I am a pregnant woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you pregnant?
      `the week of my pregnancy` IS A NUMBER @desc Which week of the pregnancy are you in?
      `I would be entitled if I were 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be entitled under s 2(a) and (b) if you were 25? (For the pregnancy route this does not change the answer: s 2(a)(2A) needs no such test.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled because I am pregnant` IS
    `s 2(a)(2A) or (d)(2) the resident is entitled under an item of the First Schedule`
        `I am a resident of Israel`
        7
        (`sch 1 item 7 a pregnant woman aged 18 or over in or after week 13` `my age in completed years` `I am a pregnant woman` `the week of my pregnancy`)
        (`helper true or not covered` `I would be entitled if I were 25`)

§§ `Am I barred or excluded? (ss 3, 3A, 3C, 4)`

-- s 3(1) to (3). Not entitled: kept in an institution wholly at public expense; a soldier in regular service, or the wife of one; a member of a body corporate
-- that is responsible for the livelihood of its members.  A flat "no" where the person is in one of the classes; otherwise the section says nothing.
@export Am I barred because I am kept at public expense, serve in the army, or belong to a collective (s 3(1) to (3))?
GIVEN `I am in an institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living in an institution?
      `my whole upkeep there is paid by the State, the Jewish Agency or a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your whole upkeep there paid for by the State treasury, the Jewish Agency for Israel or a local authority?
      `my whole upkeep there is paid by another body the regulations name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your whole upkeep there paid for by another body that the regulations name?
      `I serve regular service in the Israel Defence Forces` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you serving regular service in the Israel Defence Forces?
      `I am the wife of a person serving regular service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the wife of a person serving regular service in the Israel Defence Forces?
      `I am a member of a body corporate responsible for the livelihood of its members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a body corporate (such as a kibbutz) that is responsible for the livelihood of its members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred because I am kept at public expense, serve in the army, or belong to a collective` IS
    `s 3 the person is not entitled`
        (LIST
            (`s 3(1) the person kept in an institution at public expense is not entitled` `I am in an institution` `my whole upkeep there is paid by the State, the Jewish Agency or a local authority` `my whole upkeep there is paid by another body the regulations name`)
            (`s 3(2) the soldier in regular service and his wife are not entitled` `I serve regular service in the Israel Defence Forces` `I am the wife of a person serving regular service`)
            (`s 3(3) the member of a body corporate responsible for its members' livelihood is not entitled` `I am a member of a body corporate responsible for the livelihood of its members`))

-- s 3(4). A student at an institution the Minister set is not entitled, with exceptions: one paid under s 2(a)(4); an independent parent who was paid for 16 of the
-- 20 months before studying (unless on a second or third degree), for up to 36 months of this exception unless the Minister set a longer period.
@export Am I barred because I am a student (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `I am a student at an institution the Minister set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a student at an institution that the Minister has set by regulations, on the conditions the Minister set?
      `I am paid the allowance as a person of retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid the allowance because you have reached retirement age (s 2(a)(4))?
      `I am an independent parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an independent parent (a single parent with a child)?
      `months of allowance I was paid in the 20 months before I began to study` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the 20 months before you began to study were you paid the allowance?
      `I study for a second or third academic degree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your programme one leading to a second or third academic degree?
      `months of allowance already paid to me under this exception` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months have you already been paid the allowance as a student under this exception?
      `the Minister set a longer period and I meet its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister set a period longer than 36 months for you, and do you meet its conditions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred because I am a student` IS
    `s 3(4) the student is not entitled`
        `I am a student at an institution the Minister set`
        `I am paid the allowance as a person of retirement age`
        `I am an independent parent`
        `months of allowance I was paid in the 20 months before I began to study`
        `I study for a second or third academic degree`
        `months of allowance already paid to me under this exception`
        `the Minister set a longer period and I meet its conditions`

-- s 3A. One whose entitlement depends on s 2(a)(2), and who refused suitable work offered by the employment service, is not entitled for the month of the
-- refusal and the month after it.
@export Am I barred for the month because I refused suitable work (s 3A)?
GIVEN `my entitlement depends on being registered as unemployed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your entitlement depend on being registered as unemployed (s 2(a)(2))?
      `I refused suitable work the employment service offered me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employment service offer you suitable work, and did you refuse it?
      `calendar months since the month I refused` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar months have gone by since the month in which you refused? (0 if this month)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred for the month because I refused suitable work` IS
    `s 3A the person who refused suitable work is not entitled for the month`
        `my entitlement depends on being registered as unemployed`
        `I refused suitable work the employment service offered me`
        `calendar months since the month I refused`

-- s 3C(a). A person sentenced to imprisonment for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances is not entitled.
@export Am I barred because I was sentenced for murder in terrorist circumstances (s 3C(a))?
GIVEN `I was sentenced to imprisonment for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to imprisonment for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred because I was sentenced for murder in terrorist circumstances` IS
    `s 3C(a) the person is not entitled` `I was sentenced to imprisonment for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances`

-- s 3C(b). Subsection (a) also applies to one convicted of a security offence, sentenced to ten years or more, and released in a prisoner exchange or political
-- negotiations -- until the end of the sentence imposed.
@export Am I barred because I was released in an exchange of prisoners (s 3C(b))?
GIVEN `I was released in an exchange of prisoners or political negotiations after a conviction for a security offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you released in an exchange of Israeli prisoners, or in political negotiations, after a conviction for a security offence?
      `I was sentenced to ten years' imprisonment or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to ten years' imprisonment or more?
      `the sentence imposed on me has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sentence imposed on you ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred because I was released in an exchange of prisoners` IS
    `s 3C(b) subsection (a) applies to the person released in an exchange`
        `I was released in an exchange of prisoners or political negotiations after a conviction for a security offence`
        `I was sentenced to ten years' imprisonment or more`
        `the sentence imposed on me has ended`

-- s 4. Where there is a spouse, each spouse's entitlement also needs the other to meet the conditions of s 2 -- unless the regulations under s 4(b) exempt the person.
@export Is the spouse condition met for me (s 4)?
GIVEN `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `my spouse also meets the conditions of s 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse also meet the conditions of s 2 for entitlement?
      `the regulations under s 4(b) exempt me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under s 4(b) exempt you from this condition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the spouse condition met for me` IS
    `s 4 the spouse also meets the conditions of s 2`
        `I have a spouse`
        (JUST `my spouse also meets the conditions of s 2`)
        `the regulations under s 4(b) exempt me`

-- ss 2 to 4 together. Entitled if a ground of s 2 holds and nothing in ss 3, 3A, 3C or 4 bars it.  The grounds and bars are the person's own summary of the answers above.
@export Am I entitled to the allowance (ss 2 to 4)?
GIVEN `a ground of entitlement in s 2 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the grounds of entitlement in s 2 apply to you (the questions above)?
      `s 3 bars me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 3 bar you (kept at public expense, soldier, member of a collective, student)?
      `s 3A bars me this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 3A bar you this month (you refused suitable work)?
      `s 3C bars me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does s 3C bar you (terrorist-murder sentence or release in an exchange)?
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `my spouse also meets the conditions of s 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your spouse also meet the conditions of s 2?
      `the regulations under s 4(b) exempt me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations under s 4(b) exempt you from the spouse's condition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the allowance` IS
    `s 2 to 4 the claimant is entitled to the benefit`
        (`helper true or not covered` `a ground of entitlement in s 2 applies to me`)
        (`helper true or not covered` `s 3 bars me`)
        (`helper true or not covered` `s 3A bars me this month`)
        (`helper true or not covered` `s 3C bars me`)
        `I have a spouse`
        (`s 4 the spouse also meets the conditions of s 2` `I have a spouse` (JUST `my spouse also meets the conditions of s 2`) `the regulations under s 4(b) exempt me`)

§§ `How much would I be paid? (ss 5 to 8)`

-- s 5(a). The allowance with no income is a share of the basic amount, by family composition (the Second Schedule) and by column: A for retirement age or a survivors'
-- or dependants' allowance (in three age bands), B under 55, C from 55; less the basic amount for a child where the table says so.
@export How much would I be paid each month if I had no income (s 5(a), Second Schedule)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels? (The National Insurance Institute publishes it.)
      `the basic amount for a child now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount for a child (for the child allowance) now in force, in new shekels?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age?
      `I am paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law?
      `I am paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law?
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `the number of my children who are with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your children are with you?
      `I am a widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a widow (including a woman who is paid a survivors' or dependants' pension under the National Insurance Law)?
      `I am an independent parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an independent parent, as the Law for Assistance to Families Headed by an Independent Parent, 1992, defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much would I be paid each month if I had no income` IS
    `s 5(a) the benefit for an entitled person with no income` figures household column
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: s 5(a) reads only the basic amount and the basic amount for a child; the average wage and the pension point are not read.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, `the basic amount for a child now in force, in new shekels`, 0
        household MEANS Household OF `I have a spouse`, `the number of my children who are with me`, `I am a widow`, `I am an independent parent`
        column MEANS `s 5(a)(1) to (2) the column of the Second Schedule that applies` `my age in completed years` `I have reached retirement age` `I am paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law` `I am paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law`

-- s 5(b). With income, the allowance is the difference between the allowance but for the income and the income.
@export How much would I be paid each month given my income (s 5(b))?
GIVEN `the allowance I would get if I had no income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What would your monthly allowance be if you had no income (the answer to the question above), in new shekels?
      `my income after the deductions, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly income after the deductions of ss 12 to 12B (the answer to the income question below), in new shekels?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much would I be paid each month given my income` IS
    `s 5(b) the benefit for an entitled person who has income`
        `the allowance I would get if I had no income, in new shekels`
        `my income after the deductions, in new shekels`

-- s 5(d). A parent with a child is treated as an independent parent although the other parent is alive, if the spouse is entitled separately under the s 4(b) rules,
-- or is in prison for terrorist murder, or was sentenced for a security offence to ten years or more.
@export Am I treated as an independent parent although I have a spouse (s 5(d))?
GIVEN `I am a parent with a child with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a parent with a child with you?
      `I am entitled separately from my spouse under the Minister's rules made under s 4(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled separately from your spouse under the regulations made under s 4(b)?
      `my spouse is imprisoned for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse imprisoned for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances?
      `my spouse was sentenced for a security offence to ten years' imprisonment or more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your spouse convicted of a security offence and sentenced to ten years' imprisonment or more?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as an independent parent although I have a spouse` IS
    `s 5(d) the parent is treated as an independent parent`
        `I am a parent with a child with me`
        `I am entitled separately from my spouse under the Minister's rules made under s 4(b)`
        `my spouse is imprisoned for murder or attempted murder in terrorist circumstances`
        `my spouse was sentenced for a security offence to ten years' imprisonment or more`

-- s 5(e)(3). One entitled under s 2(e) (aged 20 to under 25) is paid the share the Ministers set, from 50% to 80%, of what would have been paid under s 5(a) and (b).
@export How much am I paid as a resident aged 20 to under 25 (s 5(e)(3))?
GIVEN `the share the Ministers set, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER @desc What share of the full allowance have the Minister of Labour and Social Affairs and the Minister of Finance set, as a fraction (for example 0.65 for 65%)?
      `the allowance I would have been paid under s 5(a) and (b), in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowance would you have been paid under s 5(a) and (b) had s 5(a) applied to you, in new shekels?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I paid as a resident aged 20 to under 25` IS
    `s 5(e)(3) the benefit for one entitled under s 2(e)`
        `the share the Ministers set, as a fraction`
        `the allowance I would have been paid under s 5(a) and (b), in new shekels`


-- s 5(f). Maintenance awarded to the person does not by itself lower the rate, where no monthly payment is due under s 2 of the Alimony (Payment Guarantee) Law
-- because the debtor did not meet its conditions or the person is not a "judgment creditor".
@export Is my allowance lowered just because maintenance was awarded to me (s 5(f))?
GIVEN `maintenance was awarded in my favour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was maintenance awarded in your favour by a court or tribunal?
      `no monthly payment is due to me under the Alimony Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no monthly payment due to you under s 2 of the Alimony (Payment Guarantee) Law, because the debtor did not meet its conditions or because you are not a "judgment creditor" under it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my allowance lowered just because maintenance was awarded to me` IS
    `s 5(f) the rate is reduced merely because maintenance was awarded`
        `maintenance was awarded in my favour`
        `no monthly payment is due to me under the Alimony Law`

-- s 5(g). A woman paid under s 5(a)(2)(b) who has reached 62 but not retirement age gets a supplement of 7.95% of the basic amount for 4 to 18 months, by year of birth (1960 to 1964).
@export Am I entitled to the supplement for a woman aged 62 or over (s 5(g))?
GIVEN `I am a woman paid the allowance as a person aged 55 or over` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a woman paid the allowance under s 5(a)(2)(b) (aged 55 or over, below retirement age)?
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age?
      `my year of birth` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year were you born?
      `complete months since I reached 62` IS A NUMBER @desc How many complete months have gone by since you reached 62?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the supplement for a woman aged 62 or over` IS
    `s 5(g) the woman is entitled to the supplement for the month`
        `I am a woman paid the allowance as a person aged 55 or over`
        `my age in completed years`
        `I have reached retirement age`
        `my year of birth`
        `complete months since I reached 62`

-- s 5(g). The supplement is 7.95% of the basic amount.
@export How much is the supplement for a woman aged 62 or over (s 5(g))?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the supplement for a woman aged 62 or over` IS
    `s 5(g) the amount of the supplement` figures
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: s 5(g) reads only the basic amount.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0, 0


-- s 6(b). Two spouses are paid one allowance; if it comes out higher on one spouse's personal data than on the other's, the higher is paid.
@export How much do we get as a couple (s 6(b))?
GIVEN `the allowance worked out on my personal data, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the couple's allowance worked out on your personal data (age and so on), in new shekels?
      `the allowance worked out on my spouse's personal data, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the couple's allowance worked out on your spouse's personal data, in new shekels?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do we get as a couple` IS
    `s 6(b) the benefit paid to the couple is the higher`
        `the allowance worked out on my personal data, in new shekels`
        `the allowance worked out on my spouse's personal data, in new shekels`

-- s 6(d). If one spouse is kept at public expense (s 3(1)), the entitled spouse is paid the couple's rate less 7.5% of the basic amount.
@export How much am I paid if my spouse is kept at public expense (s 6(d))?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels?
      `the rate for two spouses of our family composition, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the rate for two spouses of your family composition (see the allowance question above), in new shekels?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I paid if my spouse is kept at public expense` IS
    `s 6(d) the benefit paid to the entitled spouse of one excluded by s 3(1)` figures `the rate for two spouses of our family composition, in new shekels`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: s 6(d) reads only the basic amount.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0, 0


-- s 7(b). Where the Minister set a determining amount: no allowance if the income is not below it; otherwise the allowance, but not more than the gap between it and the income.
@export How much will I be paid once the determining amount is applied (s 7)?
GIVEN `my income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly income as ss 9 to 11 count it, in new shekels?
      `the determining amount that applies to me, if the Minister set one` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the determining amount that applies to you, in new shekels? (Enter -1 if the Minister has set none.)
      `my allowance before this limit, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly allowance under s 5 or 6 before this limit, in new shekels?
      `I am paid under s 5(a)(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid under s 5(a)(2)(a) (below 55)?
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age?
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be paid once the determining amount is applied` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 7(c) section 7 does not apply to the person` `I am paid under s 5(a)(2)(a)` `I have reached retirement age` `I have a spouse` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `my allowance before this limit, in new shekels`   -- s 7(c): the section does not apply, so the limit does not
        OTHERWISE `s 7(b) the benefit payable where a determining amount applies` `my income, in new shekels` amount `my allowance before this limit, in new shekels`
    WHERE
        amount MEANS IF `the determining amount that applies to me, if the Minister set one` LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the determining amount that applies to me, if the Minister set one`

-- s 8. A benefit of less than six new shekels is not paid, unless the person is paid a pension under the National Insurance Law.
@export Is my allowance withheld because it is under six shekels (s 8)?
GIVEN `my allowance for the month, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your allowance for the month, in new shekels?
      `I am paid a pension under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid a pension under the National Insurance Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my allowance withheld because it is under six shekels` IS
    `s 8 the benefit is not paid` `my allowance for the month, in new shekels` `I am paid a pension under the National Insurance Law`

§§ `How much of my income counts? (ss 9 to 12B)`

-- s 9(a). "Income" is income from the sources in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance wherever it arose, and includes the Insurance Law's benefits, payments in vocational
-- training, maintenance received, and sums deemed income from property.
@export Does this receipt count as income (s 9(a))?
GIVEN `it comes from a source listed in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it come from a source listed in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance (for example wages, business profit)?
      `it is an allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an allowance under the National Insurance Law?
      `it is a payment to me while I am in vocational training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a payment to you while you are in vocational training?
      `it is maintenance I receive for myself and my children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it maintenance (alimony) you receive for yourself and your children, including a payment under the Alimony (Payment Guarantee) Law?
      `it is a sum deemed to be income from property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a sum that counts as income from property, even if the property does not produce income?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this receipt count as income` IS
    `s 9(a) "income" the receipt is income`
        `it comes from a source listed in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance`
        `it is an allowance under the National Insurance Law`
        `it is a payment to me while I am in vocational training`
        `it is maintenance I receive for myself and my children`
        `it is a sum deemed to be income from property`

-- s 9(b1). A one-off payment under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law is treated as property; a payment in instalments is not counted as income,
-- but the claimant is treated as having the property (the one-off payment) for the months over which it is paid.
@export Is my disengagement one-off payment treated as property (s 9(b1)(1))?
GIVEN `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law?
      `it is paid to me as a one-off payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid to you as a one-off payment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disengagement one-off payment treated as property` IS
    `s 9(b1)(1) the one-off payment is treated as property`
        `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law`
        `it is paid to me as a one-off payment`

@export Is my disengagement instalment payment counted as income (s 9(b1)(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law?
      `it is paid to me in instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid to you in instalments?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disengagement instalment payment counted as income` IS
    `s 9(b1)(2)(a) the instalment payment is counted as income`
        `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law`
        `it is paid to me in instalments`

@export How much property am I treated as having while the instalments are paid (s 9(b1)(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the sum paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law?
      `it is paid to me in instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid to you in instalments?
      `the one-off payment I would have received, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the one-off payment you would have received, in new shekels?
      `the month falls within the period over which the instalments are paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the month you are asking about fall within the period over which the instalments are paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much property am I treated as having while the instalments are paid` IS
    `s 9(b1)(2)(b) the property the claimant is treated as having`
        `the sum is paid under s 3(a1)(1) of the Third Schedule of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law`
        `it is paid to me in instalments`
        `the one-off payment I would have received, in new shekels`
        `the month falls within the period over which the instalments are paid`


-- s 9(c) "property". Any property or right, here or abroad, except movables that cannot be attached, an "amount not counted", and the right to the home you live in.
@export Does this count as property (s 9(c))?
GIVEN `it is property, or a right or benefit due or held, in Israel or abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it property, real or movable, or a right or benefit due to you or held by you, in Israel or abroad?
      `it is a movable that cannot be attached under the Execution Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a movable that cannot be attached under the Execution Law?
      `it is an amount the Law does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a sum of money the Law does not count (see the next two questions)?
      `it is my right to the home I live in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it your right to hold the home you live in, not used to earn or profit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this count as property` IS
    `s 9(c) "property" the thing is property`
        `it is property, or a right or benefit due or held, in Israel or abroad`
        `it is a movable that cannot be attached under the Execution Law`
        `it is an amount the Law does not count`
        `it is my right to the home I live in`

-- s 9(c) "amount not counted", limb (1). Money up to four times the basic amount; six times for one with a child with them or a spouse.
@export Is my money left out of my property (s 9(c), first kind)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels?
      `the total sum of money I hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total sum of money you hold, in new shekels?
      `I have a child with me or a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a child with you, or a spouse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my money left out of my property` IS
    `s 9(c) "amount not counted" (1) the sum of money is not counted` figures `the total sum of money I hold` `I have a child with me or a spouse`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: this rule reads only the basic amount.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0, 0

-- s 9(c) "amount not counted", limb (2). A sum received for selling the home you lived in, for 12 months or until you buy another home, whichever is earlier.
@export Is the money I got for selling my home left out of my property today (s 9(c), second kind)?
GIVEN `the sum was received for selling a home I lived in, or as compensation under the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the sum received for selling a home you lived in, or as compensation under sub-chapter A of chapter 5 of the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law?
      `the day I received the sum` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you receive the sum?
      `today` IS A DATE @desc What is today's date?
      `I bought another home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you bought another home to live in?
      `the day I bought it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you buy it? (Ignored if you have not bought one.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the money I got for selling my home left out of my property today` IS
    `s 9(c) "amount not counted" (2) the sale proceeds are not counted on the day`
        `the sum was received for selling a home I lived in, or as compensation under the Disengagement Plan Implementation Law`
        `the day I received the sum`
        `today`
        (IF `I bought another home` THEN JUST `the day I bought it` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 9A. Two vehicles, or one worth more than the Minister's amount (for one paid under s 5(a)(1): more than the updated 60,000 shekels), takes away entitlement -- unless
-- an exception in s 9A(c) holds (medical treatment, disability, mobility, a child's pension, a deposited licence).
@export Does owning a vehicle take away my entitlement (s 9A(b))?
GIVEN `the number of vehicles I own` IS A NUMBER @desc How many vehicles do you own? (Count one you drive as an owner even if it is not registered in your name.)
      `the value of my most valuable vehicle, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of your most valuable vehicle, in new shekels?
      `the Minister's limit on a vehicle's value for me, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What limit on a vehicle's value has the Minister set for people in your situation, in new shekels? (Enter -1 if none.)
      `I am paid under s 5(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid under s 5(a)(1) (retirement age, or an old-age, survivors' or dependants' allowance)?
      `the updated figure of 60,000 shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the updated figure of 60,000 new shekels that applies to people paid under s 5(a)(1)? (The Institute publishes it.)
      `an exception in s 9A(c) holds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the exceptions in s 9A(c) apply to you: needing the vehicle for medical treatment, a leg disability, being a disabled person's driving licensee, a child's pension, a deposited licence while ill, or an idle tractor on an inactive farm?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does owning a vehicle take away my entitlement` IS
    `s 9A(b) the claimant is not entitled because of their vehicles`
        `the number of vehicles I own`
        `the value of my most valuable vehicle, in new shekels`
        (IF `the Minister's limit on a vehicle's value for me, in new shekels` LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the Minister's limit on a vehicle's value for me, in new shekels`)
        `I am paid under s 5(a)(1)`
        `the updated figure of 60,000 shekels`
        `an exception in s 9A(c) holds`

-- s 9A(b1). A claimant with one vehicle within the s 9A(b) limits has a deduction made from the allowance if the vehicle is worth more than 10,309 new shekels (as updated) --
-- unless the claimant works; the Minister sets the amount.
@export How much is deducted from my allowance for my one vehicle (s 9A(b1))?
GIVEN `I own one vehicle worth no more than the amounts in s 9A(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you own one vehicle, worth no more than the amounts in s 9A(b)?
      `I am paid under s 5(a)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid under s 5(a)(1) (retirement age, or an old-age, survivors' or dependants' allowance)?
      `I work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work?
      `the value of my vehicle, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of your vehicle, in new shekels?
      `the updated figure of 10,309 shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the updated figure of 10,309 new shekels? (The Institute publishes it.)
      `the Minister set a deduction for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister set, by regulations, a deduction for people in your situation?
      `the deduction the Minister set, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What deduction has the Minister set, in new shekels? (Ignored if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted from my allowance for my one vehicle` IS
    `s 9A(b1) the deduction from the benefit for the vehicle`
        `I own one vehicle worth no more than the amounts in s 9A(b)`
        `I am paid under s 5(a)(1)`
        `I work`
        `the value of my vehicle, in new shekels`
        `the updated figure of 10,309 shekels`
        (IF `the Minister set a deduction for me` THEN JUST `the deduction the Minister set, in new shekels` ELSE NOTHING)


-- s 9A(c)(2). The vehicle is needed for medical treatment outside the home under a plan set in advance, or at least 6 times a month over more than 90 days.
@export Does my need for a vehicle for medical treatment lift the vehicle limits (s 9A(c)(2))?
GIVEN `I or a family member need the vehicle for medical treatment outside the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you or a family member you drive to treatment need the vehicle for medical treatment given outside the home?
      `the treatment is under a plan set in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the treatment under a plan set in advance?
      `treatments in a month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many treatments are there in a month?
      `consecutive days over which they are given` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many consecutive days are they given?
      `I meet the Minister's rules for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the rules and conditions the Minister set for this exception?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my need for a vehicle for medical treatment lift the vehicle limits` IS
    `s 9A(c)(2) the vehicle is needed for medical treatment`
        `I or a family member need the vehicle for medical treatment outside the home`
        `the treatment is under a plan set in advance`
        `treatments in a month`
        `consecutive days over which they are given`
        `I meet the Minister's rules for this`

-- s 9A(c). The vehicle limits do not apply where (2) it is needed for medical treatment, (3) the claimant, spouse or child is disabled in the legs and paid a vehicle-maintenance payment or
-- found to need transport, (3A) the claimant is the driving licensee of a disabled person, (4) a pension is paid for the claimant's child, (5) the licence is deposited while the claimant is ill (six months),
-- or the vehicle is an idle tractor of an inactive farm.
@export Does an exception in s 9A(c) let me keep my vehicle (s 9A(c))?
GIVEN `I or a family member need the vehicle for medical treatment outside the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you or a family member need the vehicle for medical treatment given outside the home?
      `the treatment is under a plan set in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the treatment under a plan set in advance?
      `treatments in a month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many treatments are there in a month?
      `consecutive days over which they are given` IS A NUMBER @desc Over how many consecutive days are they given?
      `I meet the Minister's rules for the medical exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the rules and conditions the Minister set for this exception?
      `I, my spouse or my child is disabled in the legs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, your spouse or your child disabled in the legs?
      `they are paid a vehicle-maintenance payment from the State treasury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they paid a vehicle-maintenance payment from the State treasury?
      `an authorised doctor found that they need transport because of that disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a doctor authorised under s 208 of the Insurance Law find that they need transport because of that disability?
      `I meet the Minister's rules for the leg-disability exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the rules, conditions and period the Minister set for this exception?
      `I am the driving licensee of a disabled person under the mobility agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the driving licensee of a disabled person under the mobility agreement made under s 9 of the Insurance Law?
      `a pension is paid for my child under sub-chapter F of chapter 9 of the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a pension paid for your child under sub-chapter F of chapter 9 of the National Insurance Law?
      `my vehicle licence is deposited with the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your vehicle licence deposited with the licensing authority?
      `I cannot work in any work because of illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you not work in any work because of illness?
      `the day I submitted my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you submit your claim?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `the vehicle is a tractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vehicle a tractor, as the Traffic Regulations define it?
      `the tractor is not in use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the tractor not in use?
      `I have a farm that is not active` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a farm that is not active?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does an exception in s 9A(c) let me keep my vehicle` IS
    `s 9A(c) one of the exceptions holds`
        (LIST
            `s 9A(c)(2) the vehicle is needed for medical treatment` `I or a family member need the vehicle for medical treatment outside the home` `the treatment is under a plan set in advance` `treatments in a month` `consecutive days over which they are given` `I meet the Minister's rules for the medical exception`,
            `s 9A(c)(3) the person disabled in the legs` `I, my spouse or my child is disabled in the legs` `they are paid a vehicle-maintenance payment from the State treasury` `an authorised doctor found that they need transport because of that disability` `I meet the Minister's rules for the leg-disability exception`,
            `s 9A(c)(3A) the driving licensee of a disabled person` `I am the driving licensee of a disabled person under the mobility agreement`,
            `s 9A(c)(4) a pension is paid for the claimant's child` `a pension is paid for my child under sub-chapter F of chapter 9 of the National Insurance Law`,
            `s 9A(c)(5)(a) the claimant is ill and the licence is deposited` `my vehicle licence is deposited with the authority` `I cannot work in any work because of illness` `the day I submitted my claim` `the day I am asking about`,
            `s 9A(c)(5)(b) the tractor of an inactive farm` `my vehicle licence is deposited with the authority` `the vehicle is a tractor` `the tractor is not in use` `I have a farm that is not active`)


-- s 10. Not counted as income: a child allowance under chapter 4 of the Insurance Law; grants to soldiers and their families under the Discharged Soldiers (Return to Work)
-- Law; any other income the Minister set by regulations.
@export Is this receipt left out of my income (s 10)?
GIVEN `it is a child allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a child allowance under chapter 4 of the National Insurance Law?
      `it is a grant to a soldier or a soldier's family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a grant to a soldier or to a member of a soldier's family under the Discharged Soldiers (Return to Work) Law?
      `the Minister set it by regulations as not counted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister set, by regulations, that this kind of income is not counted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this receipt left out of my income` IS
    `s 10 the receipt is not counted as income`
        `it is a child allowance under the National Insurance Law`
        `it is a grant to a soldier or a soldier's family member`
        `the Minister set it by regulations as not counted`

-- s 11. A person with a spouse has the income of both added together, unless the Minister provided otherwise.
@export How much income is counted for a couple (s 11)?
GIVEN `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `my own income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your own monthly income, in new shekels?
      `my spouse's income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your spouse's monthly income, in new shekels?
      `the Minister provided otherwise for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister provided otherwise for people in your situation, in regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much income is counted for a couple` IS
    `s 11 the income of a person with a spouse`
        `I have a spouse`
        `my own income, in new shekels`
        `my spouse's income, in new shekels`
        `the Minister provided otherwise for me`

-- ss 12, 12A, 12B. From the income that counts, deductions are taken, by the age and kind of allowance: s 12B for those paid under s 5(a)(1), s 12A under 55, s 12 for 55 or
-- over (and for employed people with reduced capacity for work).  The deductions are shares of the average wage, taken from each earner's earnings and from pension income.
@export How much of our income counts after the deductions (ss 12, 12A, 12B)?
GIVEN `the average wage now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average wage now in force, in new shekels? (The National Insurance Institute publishes it.)
      `my age in completed years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age?
      `I am paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law?
      `I am paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law?
      `I am entitled to an adjusted minimum wage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an adjusted minimum wage under s 17(b) of the Minimum Wage Law?
      `item 17 of the First Schedule applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does item 17 of the First Schedule (a sheltered workshop) apply to you?
      `I am a rehabilitee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a rehabilitee as the Rights of Persons with Disabilities Employed as Rehabilitees (temporary provision) Law defines?
      `I am paid a survivors' or dependants' pension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid a survivors' pension under the National Insurance Law or a dependants' pension under sub-chapter H of its chapter 2?
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `the number of my children who are with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your children are with you?
      `I am an independent parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an independent parent (a single parent with a child)?
      `I am a widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a widow?
      `my earnings, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your monthly earnings from work and wage-replacement payments (the "tagmul" of s 12(c)), in new shekels?
      `my spouse's earnings, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your spouse's monthly earnings of the same kind, in new shekels? (0 if none.)
      `our pension income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly income from a pension paid under an enactment, foreign law, collective agreement or employment contract (not a National Insurance pension), in new shekels?
      `our other income, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your monthly income from any other source that counts, in new shekels?
      `I am an individual entitled under s 30A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a single person entitled to the benefit under s 30A (a "former entitled" person)?
      `we are both entitled under s 30A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you and your spouse both entitled to the benefit under s 30A?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of our income counts after the deductions` IS
    asum (LIST under12, under12A, under12B)
    WHERE
        under12 MEANS `s 12 the income after the deductions` figures earners `our pension income, in new shekels` `our other income, in new shekels` family `I am an independent parent` section12
        under12A MEANS `s 12A the income after the deductions` figures earners `our pension income, in new shekels` `our other income, in new shekels` family `I am an independent parent` rate section12A
        under12B MEANS `s 12B the income after the deductions` figures earners `our pension income, in new shekels` `our other income, in new shekels` family `I am an independent parent` section12B
        -- Placeholder: ss 12 to 12B read only the average wage.
        figures MEANS Figures OF 0, `the average wage now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0
        earners MEANS LIST `my earnings, in new shekels`, `my spouse's earnings, in new shekels`
        family MEANS `I have a spouse` OR `the number of my children who are with me` AT LEAST 1
        column MEANS `s 5(a)(1) to (2) the column of the Second Schedule that applies` `my age in completed years` `I have reached retirement age` `I am paid an old-age or survivors' allowance under the National Insurance Law` `I am paid a dependants' allowance under the National Insurance Law`
        reduced MEANS `s 12(c) "employed with reduced capacity for work" the person is one` `I am entitled to an adjusted minimum wage` `item 17 of the First Schedule applies to me` `I am a rehabilitee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        section12 MEANS `s 12(a) the section applies to the claimant` (column EQUALS `column C from 55`) reduced `I am paid a survivors' or dependants' pension`
        section12A MEANS `s 12A(a) the section applies to the claimant` (column EQUALS `column B under 55`) reduced
        section12B MEANS `s 12B(a) the section applies to the claimant` (column EQUALS `column A under 70` OR column EQUALS `column A from 70 to under 80` OR column EQUALS `column A from 80`)
        rate MEANS `sch 3 the rate of deduction for the household` household `I am an individual entitled under s 30A` `we are both entitled under s 30A`
        household MEANS Household OF `I have a spouse`, `the number of my children who are with me`, `I am a widow`, `I am an independent parent`

§§ `From when am I paid? (s 14)`

-- s 14(a). Paid only from the 1st of the month in which the claim was submitted -- unless a regulation of the Minister lets payment run from an earlier day.
@export From which day will I be paid (s 14(a))?
GIVEN `the day I submitted my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you submit your claim to the National Insurance Institute?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From which day will I be paid` IS
    `s 14(a) the first day for which the benefit is paid` `the day I submitted my claim`

@export Will I be paid for a day before the month of my claim (s 14(a))?
GIVEN `the day I submitted my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you submit your claim to the National Insurance Institute?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `a regulation of the Minister lets me be paid from an earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation of the Minister let you be paid from an earlier day?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be paid for a day before the month of my claim` IS
    `s 14(a) the day is within the period for which the benefit is paid`
        `the day I submitted my claim`
        `the day I am asking about`
        `a regulation of the Minister lets me be paid from an earlier day`

-- s 14(c)(1). One who reached retirement age and is found entitled under s 2(a)(4) also for a period before the claim is paid for it too: up to the 12 months just before
-- the month of the claim, and not for a month in which they had not reached retirement age.
@export Will I be paid for a month before my claim if I have reached retirement age (s 14(c)(1))?
GIVEN `I have reached retirement age and I am found entitled under s 2(a)(4) for an earlier period too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you reached retirement age, and were you found entitled under s 2(a)(4) for an earlier period as well?
      `how many months before the month of my claim the month is` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months before the month of your claim is the month you are asking about? (1 is the month just before.)
      `I had reached retirement age in that month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you reached retirement age in that month?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will I be paid for a month before my claim if I have reached retirement age` IS
    `s 14(c)(1) the benefit is paid for a month before the month of the claim`
        `I have reached retirement age and I am found entitled under s 2(a)(4) for an earlier period too`
        `how many months before the month of my claim the month is`
        `I had reached retirement age in that month`

§§ `If I leave Israel (s 14A)`

-- s 14A(a) to (c). For a person below retirement age (and whose spouse is): no allowance for a month spent wholly abroad; none for the month of exit and of return if they left
-- another time that year or were not entitled the month before; and, for those on s 2(a)(2) or (3) in training, none for those months unless the condition held all month.
@export Is my allowance withheld for a month I spent wholly outside Israel (s 14A(a))?
GIVEN `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or your spouse reached retirement age?
      `I left Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave Israel?
      `I was outside Israel on every day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you outside Israel on every day of the month?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my allowance withheld for a month I spent wholly outside Israel` IS
    `s 14A(a) the benefit is not paid for the month`
        `my spouse or I have reached retirement age`
        `I left Israel`
        `I was outside Israel on every day of the month`

@export Is my allowance withheld for the month I left and the month I came back (s 14A(b), (c))?
GIVEN `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or your spouse reached retirement age?
      `this is the month I left or the month I came back` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the month you are asking about the month you left Israel or the month you came back?
      `I had left Israel another time earlier in the same calendar year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before leaving, had you left Israel another time in the same calendar year?
      `I was entitled the month before I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to the allowance for the calendar month before the month you left?
      `I am entitled under s 2(a)(2), or under s 2(a)(3) while in training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your entitlement under s 2(a)(2), or under s 2(a)(3) while you are in training?
      `my s 2(a)(2) or (3) condition held for the whole month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the condition of s 2(a)(2) or (3) hold for you throughout the whole month?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my allowance withheld for the month I left and the month I came back` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 14A(b) the benefit is not paid for the month of exit and the month of return` `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` `this is the month I left or the month I came back` `I had left Israel another time earlier in the same calendar year` `I was entitled the month before I left` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE   -- s 14A(b): not paid
        OTHERWISE `s 14A(c) the benefit is not paid for the month of exit and the month of return` `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` `I am entitled under s 2(a)(2), or under s 2(a)(3) while in training` `this is the month I left or the month I came back` `my s 2(a)(2) or (3) condition held for the whole month` (`s 14A(b) the benefit is not paid for the month of exit and the month of return` `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` `this is the month I left or the month I came back` `I had left Israel another time earlier in the same calendar year` `I was entitled the month before I left` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- s 14A(c1). For a person who, or whose spouse, has reached retirement age: no allowance for the month of the fourth exit in a year, every month with a day abroad if more than
-- four exits, and, if fewer than four, the months holding the 73rd to 100th day abroad, or every month with a day abroad if more than 100 days.
@export Is my allowance withheld for a month in which I was abroad, if I or my spouse has reached retirement age (s 14A(c1))?
GIVEN `my spouse or I have reached retirement age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you or your spouse reached retirement age?
      `how many times my spouse and I together left Israel this calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times did you and your spouse together leave Israel this calendar year?
      `the total days we were outside Israel this calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days in all were you and your spouse outside Israel this calendar year?
      `the days we were outside Israel before this month in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were you outside Israel before this month in the calendar year?
      `the days we were outside Israel in this month` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were you outside Israel in this month?
      `this is the month of the fourth exit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the month in which you were outside Israel, wholly or partly, for the fourth time this year?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my allowance withheld for a month in which I was abroad, if I or my spouse has reached retirement age` IS
    `s 14A(c1) the benefit is not paid for the month`
        `my spouse or I have reached retirement age`
        `how many times my spouse and I together left Israel this calendar year`
        `the total days we were outside Israel this calendar year`
        `the days we were outside Israel before this month in the year`
        `the days we were outside Israel in this month`
        `this is the month of the fourth exit`

-- s 14A(d). The bans in (a), (b) and (c1) do not apply to one who was entitled the month before and needs medical treatment abroad, or accompanies a sick family member who does.
@export Does a medical need abroad save my allowance (s 14A(d))?
GIVEN `I was entitled the month before I left` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to the allowance for the calendar month before the month you left?
      `I need medical treatment outside Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you need medical treatment outside Israel (a health service under s 11 of the State Health Insurance Law)?
      `I am entitled because I care for a family member and I accompany them for treatment abroad` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled because you mainly care for your son, daughter, spouse or parent, and do you accompany them to medical treatment outside Israel?
      `I meet the Minister's rules for this` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the rules, conditions and period the Minister set for this exception?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a medical need abroad save my allowance` IS
    `s 14A(d) subsections (a), (b) and (c1) do not apply to the person`
        `I was entitled the month before I left`
        `I need medical treatment outside Israel`
        `I am entitled because I care for a family member and I accompany them for treatment abroad`
        `I meet the Minister's rules for this`

-- s 14A(f)(1). After 183 days or more abroad within 12 consecutive months, a person is treated as outside Israel until 12 consecutive months with 183 days in Israel have gone by --
-- unless they told the Institute in time, or were abroad for treatment under s 11 of the State Health Insurance Law.
@export Am I treated as living abroad after a long stay (s 14A(f))?
GIVEN `the days I stayed outside Israel within 12 consecutive months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days did you stay outside Israel within 12 consecutive months?
      `12 consecutive months with 183 days in Israel have gone by since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have 12 consecutive months gone by since, in which you stayed in Israel for at least 183 days?
      `I told the Institute in time of leaving, my absence and my return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell the Institute, in time and in the manner the Minister set, that you were leaving, how long you would be away, and when you returned?
      `I stayed abroad for medical treatment under the State Health Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you stay abroad to receive medical treatment under s 11 of the State Health Insurance Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as living abroad after a long stay` IS
    `s 14A(f)(1) the entitled person is treated as outside Israel`
        `the days I stayed outside Israel within 12 consecutive months`
        `12 consecutive months with 183 days in Israel have gone by since`
        (`s 14A(f)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply to the person` `I told the Institute in time of leaving, my absence and my return` `I stayed abroad for medical treatment under the State Health Insurance Law`)

-- s 14A(e). If one spouse is abroad and not entitled because of s 14A, the entitled spouse in Israel is paid at the rate for an individual of their family composition.
@export How much does my spouse in Israel get while I am abroad (s 14A(e))?
GIVEN `I am abroad and not entitled because of s 14A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you abroad and not entitled to the allowance because of s 14A?
      `my spouse is entitled and is in Israel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your spouse entitled to the allowance, and in Israel?
      `the allowance for an individual of my spouse's family composition, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the allowance for an individual of your spouse's family composition (see the allowance question above), in new shekels?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does my spouse in Israel get while I am abroad` IS
    `s 14A(e) the benefit paid to the spouse in Israel`
        `I am abroad and not entitled because of s 14A`
        `my spouse is entitled and is in Israel`
        (JUST `the allowance for an individual of my spouse's family composition, in new shekels`)

§§ `Other payments`

-- s 14B. A heating grant of 6.4% of the basic amount for one entitled for October, November or December who has reached retirement age by then.
@export How much is the heating grant I am entitled to (s 14B)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels?
      `I am entitled for October` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the allowance for October?
      `I am entitled for November` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the allowance for November?
      `I am entitled for December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the allowance for December?
      `the first month of this year by which I had reached retirement age` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month of this calendar year did you reach retirement age? (Enter 0 if before this year, 13 if not yet this year.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the heating grant I am entitled to` IS
    `s 14B the heating grant` figures `I am entitled for October` `I am entitled for November` `I am entitled for December` `the first month of this year by which I had reached retirement age`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the heating grant reads only the basic amount.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0, 0

-- s 15(a). On the death of an entitled person who was paid, the grant goes to the surviving spouse, or if none to one of the children.
@export Who is paid the grant if the person receiving the allowance dies (s 15(a))?
GIVEN `the person who died was being paid the allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the person who died being paid the allowance?
      `they had a spouse when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they have a spouse when they died?
      `they have a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they have a child?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Death grant recipient`
DECIDE `Who is paid the grant if the person receiving the allowance dies` IS
    `s 15(a) who is paid the death grant`
        `the person who died was being paid the allowance`
        `they had a spouse when they died`
        `they have a child`

-- s 15(a) as amended in force from 1 January 2006 (SH 1892 p.474 s 67(4)): the grant equals the basic amount.  Assumed, not in the text: the basic amount in force on the day of death (NOTES.md, F20).
@export How much is the grant on death (s 15(a))?
GIVEN `the basic amount in force on the day of death, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the basic amount in force on the day the person died, in new shekels?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the grant on death` IS
    `s 15(a) the amount of the death grant`
        `the basic amount in force on the day of death, in new shekels`

@export How many of the two grants on death may I receive (s 15(b))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to the grant on death under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the grant on death under this Law?
      `I am entitled to the grant on death under s 310 of the National Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the grant on death under s 310 of the National Insurance Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of the two grants on death may I receive` IS
    `s 15(b) how many of the two grants the person may receive`
        `I am entitled to the grant on death under this Law`
        `I am entitled to the grant on death under s 310 of the National Insurance Law`

§§ `If I was paid more in the past (s 30A, s 30)`

-- s 30A(a). A "former entitled person" is one who is not now paid under s 5(a)(1) or (2)(b) but was paid an increased benefit for December 2002.
@export Am I a "former entitled person" (s 30A(a))?
GIVEN `I am now paid under s 5(a)(1) or (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you now paid under s 5(a)(1) (retirement age or an Insurance Law pension) or s 5(a)(2)(b) (aged 55 or over)?
      `I was paid an increased benefit for December 2002 under the old wording` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid an increased benefit for December 2002 under s 5(a)(2), (2A) or (d), or s 5(c), as they read before the 2002 and 2003 Arrangements Laws?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a former entitled person` IS
    `s 30A(a) the person is a former entitled person`
        `I am now paid under s 5(a)(1) or (2)(b)`
        `I was paid an increased benefit for December 2002 under the old wording`

@export How much do I get as a former entitled person (s 30A(b))?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels?
      `I have a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a spouse?
      `the number of my children who are with me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your children are with you?
      `I am a widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a widow (including a woman who is paid a survivors' or dependants' pension under the National Insurance Law)?
      `I am an independent parent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an independent parent, as the Law for Assistance to Families Headed by an Independent Parent, 1992, defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I get as a former entitled person` IS
    `s 30A(b) the benefit of a former entitled person` figures household
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: s 30A(b) reads only the basic amount.
        figures MEANS Figures OF `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`, 0, 0, 0
        household MEANS Household OF `I have a spouse`, `the number of my children who are with me`, `I am a widow`, `I am an independent parent`

@export Do I go back to the ordinary rate after six months without the allowance (s 30A(c))?
GIVEN `consecutive months I was not entitled since the 2003 Arrangements Law took effect` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many consecutive months were you not entitled to the benefit, after the 2003 Arrangements Law took effect?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I go back to the ordinary rate after six months without the allowance` IS
    `s 30A(c) subsection (b) does not apply and s 5(a) applies` `consecutive months I was not entitled since the 2003 Arrangements Law took effect`

-- s 30(b). One who was supported immediately before becoming entitled gets at least the last support, unless the lower amount comes only from the Law's income rules.
@export How much will I be paid if I was supported before I became entitled (s 30(b))?
GIVEN `I got support immediately before I became entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive support immediately before you became entitled to the allowance?
      `the last support paid to me, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the last support paid to you, in new shekels?
      `the allowance the Law gives me, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowance does this Law give you, in new shekels?
      `it is lower only because of the Law's rules for counting income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the allowance lower than your last support only because of this Law's rules for counting income?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be paid if I was supported before I became entitled` IS
    `s 30(b) the benefit paid, not less than the last support`
        `I got support immediately before I became entitled`
        `the last support paid to me, in new shekels`
        `the allowance the Law gives me, in new shekels`
        `it is lower only because of the Law's rules for counting income`

§§ `What must I do to get and keep the allowance? (ss 13, 17(b), 19 to 21, Fifth Schedule)`

-- s 13(a). A claim for a benefit is submitted to the National Insurance Institute.
@export Where do I submit my claim (s 13(a))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Where do I submit my claim` IS
    `s 13(a) where a claim for a benefit is submitted`

-- s 17(b). Someone paid a benefit must help the Institute to recover compensation for it from a person liable for maintenance, and must not harm that right.
@export Am I failing my duty to help the Institute recover compensation (s 17(b))?
GIVEN `I refused or failed to give help or to take a reasonable step to assist the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse or fail to give help, or to take a reasonable step, when the Institute asked for your help to claim compensation from someone liable for your maintenance?
      `I did an act liable to harm the Institute's right to compensation or to prevent its realisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do something liable to harm the Institute's right to claim that compensation, or to prevent it being realised?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I failing my duty to help the Institute recover compensation` IS
    `s 17(b) the recipient is in breach of the duty`
        `I refused or failed to give help or to take a reasonable step to assist the Institute`
        `I did an act liable to harm the Institute's right to compensation or to prevent its realisation`

-- s 19(a). A claimant or recipient must give the Institute the information and documents it demands, undergo the examination it demands, and appear before the person it names.
@export Have I met the Institute's demand (s 19(a))?
GIVEN `the Institute demanded information or documents from me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Institute demand information or documents from you?
      `the Institute demanded that I undergo a medical or other expert examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Institute demand that you undergo a medical or other expert examination?
      `the Institute demanded that I appear before a person it named` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Institute demand that you appear before a person it named?
      `I have complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you done everything the Institute demanded?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the Institute's demand` IS
    `s 19(a) the claimant or recipient has met the Institute's demand`
        `the Institute demanded information or documents from me`
        `the Institute demanded that I undergo a medical or other expert examination`
        `the Institute demanded that I appear before a person it named`
        `I have complied`

-- s 20. A recipient must tell the Institute in writing of a change in family status, income or another matter, within 60 days of the change, if the change may affect entitlement or rate.
@export Did I tell the Institute of the change in time (s 20)?
GIVEN `the change is in my family status, my income or a matter I gave the Institute information about, or one it said it needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change in your family status, your income, or another matter you gave the Institute information about, or one the Institute told you it needs for the benefit?
      `the change may affect my entitlement or rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the change affect whether you are entitled, or how much you are paid?
      `I gave the Institute written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the Institute written notice of the change?
      `days from the change to my written notice` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the change did you give written notice? (Ignored if you have not given it.)
      `days since the change` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the change?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I tell the Institute of the change in time` IS
    `s 20 the recipient notified the change in time`
        `the change is in my family status, my income or a matter I gave the Institute information about, or one it said it needs`
        `the change may affect my entitlement or rate`
        (IF `I gave the Institute written notice` THEN JUST `days from the change to my written notice` ELSE NOTHING)
        `days since the change`

-- s 21(b). One who is questioned, or on whose premises an inspection is made, must give a full and true answer to every question put.
@export Have I met my duty to answer the Institute's questions (s 21(b))?
GIVEN `I answered every question put to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you answer every question put to you?
      `my answers were full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your answers full?
      `my answers were true` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your answers true?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duty to answer the Institute's questions` IS
    `s 21(b) the person met the duty to answer`
        `I answered every question put to me`
        `my answers were full`
        `my answers were true`

-- s 21(c). One who has or knows of information about a claimant's or recipient's income or property must give the details within 30 days of an authorised employee's demand.
@export Did I give the Institute the details it demanded in time (s 21(c))?
GIVEN `I have or know of information about the income or property of a claimant or recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or know of, information about the income or property of someone who claims or receives a benefit?
      `an authorised employee of the Institute demanded the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an authorised employee of the Institute demand the details?
      `I gave the details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the details?
      `days from the demand to my giving the details` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the demand did you give them? (Ignored if you have not.)
      `days since the demand` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days have passed since the demand?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I give the Institute the details it demanded in time` IS
    `s 21(c) the person gave the details in time`
        `I have or know of information about the income or property of a claimant or recipient`
        `an authorised employee of the Institute demanded the details`
        (IF `I gave the details` THEN JUST `days from the demand to my giving the details` ELSE NOTHING)
        `days since the demand`

-- Fifth Schedule, Part B and Part A. A recipient must report these details (Part B); Part A items 1, 3 and 4 add a threshold on the change, items 2, 5 to 7, 9 and 10 have none, item 8 names who counts.
@export Must I report this detail to the Institute (Fifth Schedule, Part B)?
GIVEN `the detail` IS A `Sch 5 detail` @desc Which detail is it: an account balance, a right in real estate, income from work, income from other sources, the address of residence, foreign citizenship, entering and leaving Israel, living under one roof with a spouse or another listed person, money received directly from the maintenance debtor, or a later maintenance judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report this detail to the Institute` IS
    `sch 5 part B the detail is required` `the detail`

@export Must I report a change in my account balance (Fifth Schedule, Part A item 1)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels? (Fifth Schedule counts it as para (3) of the Insurance Law's definition has it.)
      `I am reporting only whether I have a balance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reporting only whether an account balance exists, not a change in it?
      `the change in the balance, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc How large is the change in the balance, in new shekels?
      `I have a child with me or a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a child with you, or a spouse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report a change in my account balance` IS
    `sch 5 part A item 1 the account balance must be reported`
        `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`
        `I am reporting only whether I have a balance`
        `the change in the balance, in new shekels`
        `I have a child with me or a spouse`

@export Must I report a change in my income from work (Fifth Schedule, Part A item 3)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels? (Fifth Schedule counts it as para (3) of the Insurance Law's definition has it.)
      `I am reporting the amount of my income from work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reporting the amount of your income from work, not a change in it?
      `the change in my income from work, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc How large is the change in your income from work, in new shekels?
      `I have a child with me or a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a child with you, or a spouse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report a change in my income from work` IS
    `sch 5 part A item 3 the income from work must be reported`
        `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`
        `I am reporting the amount of my income from work`
        `the change in my income from work, in new shekels`
        `I have a child with me or a spouse`

@export Must I report a change in my income from other sources (Fifth Schedule, Part A item 4)?
GIVEN `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the basic amount now in force, in new shekels? (Fifth Schedule counts it as para (3) of the Insurance Law's definition has it.)
      `I am reporting whether I have income from other sources` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reporting whether you have income from other sources, not a change in it?
      `the change in my income from other sources, in new shekels` IS A NUMBER @desc How large is the change in your income from other sources, in new shekels?
      `I have a child with me or a spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a child with you, or a spouse?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report a change in my income from other sources` IS
    `sch 5 part A item 4 the income from other sources must be reported`
        `the basic amount now in force, in new shekels`
        `I am reporting whether I have income from other sources`
        `the change in my income from other sources, in new shekels`
        `I have a child with me or a spouse`

@export Must I report that I live under one roof with this person (Fifth Schedule, Part A item 8)?
GIVEN `the person is my spouse, including one I married under the law of a foreign state` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person your spouse, including one you married under the law of a foreign state?
      `the person is a parent of one of my children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a parent of one of your children?
      `I have a joint bank account, or a joint right in real estate or a vehicle, with the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a joint bank account, or a joint right in real estate or a vehicle, with the person?
      `I have an agreement with the person to share income or expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a property agreement or another agreement with the person to share income or expenses?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I report that I live under one roof with this person` IS
    `sch 5 part A item 8 living with the person must be reported`
        `the person is my spouse, including one I married under the law of a foreign state`
        `the person is a parent of one of my children`
        `I have a joint bank account, or a joint right in real estate or a vehicle, with the person`
        `I have an agreement with the person to share income or expenses`

@export What warning must a notice about the Fifth Schedule carry (Fifth Schedule, Part C)?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What warning must a notice about the Fifth Schedule carry` IS
    `sch 5 part C the warning the notice must carry`

§§ `Can an official come in, and who sees my information? (ss 21, 21A)`

-- s 21(a). An employee the Institute's administration authorised may enter, at a reasonable hour, a place where there is reasonable ground to believe information is kept, to carry out the Law.
@export May an Institute employee come into my premises (s 21(a))?
GIVEN `the employee is authorised by the Institute's administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employee authorised by the Institute's administration?
      `the entry is at a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entry at a reasonable time?
      `there is reasonable ground to believe information needed to establish income or another detail is there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there reasonable ground to believe that information needed to establish income, or another detail, is in the place?
      `the entry is to carry out this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entry made to carry out this Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an Institute employee come into my premises` IS
    `s 21(a) the employee may enter the place`
        `the employee is authorised by the Institute's administration`
        `the entry is at a reasonable time`
        `there is reasonable ground to believe information needed to establish income or another detail is there`
        `the entry is to carry out this Law`

@export May an Institute employee force their way in (s 21(a))?
GIVEN `the place is where I live` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place a residence?
      `the employee has an order of a Magistrates' Court judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the employee have an order from a judge of a Magistrates' Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May an Institute employee force their way in` IS
    `s 21(a) the employee may enter by force`
        `the place is where I live`
        `the employee has an order of a Magistrates' Court judge`

-- s 21A. Information given to the Institute under s 326(f) of the Insurance Law may be used for s 3C, 5(d) or 6(e); s 326(g) of the Insurance Law applies to a security terror offence.
@export May the Institute use information it holds about me for this Law (s 21A(1))?
GIVEN `the information was given to the Institute under s 326(f) of the Insurance Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information given to the Institute under s 326(f) of the Insurance Law?
      `the use is for the purposes of s 3C, 5(d) or 6(e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for the purposes of s 3C, 5(d) or 6(e) of this Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Institute use information it holds about me for this Law` IS
    `s 21A(1) the Institute may use the information`
        `the information was given to the Institute under s 326(f) of the Insurance Law`
        `the use is for the purposes of s 3C, 5(d) or 6(e)`

@export Does s 326(g) of the Insurance Law apply to my offence (s 21A(2))?
GIVEN `the offence is a security terror offence as s 326(g) of the Insurance Law has it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence a security terror offence, as s 326(g) of the Insurance Law has it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 326(g) of the Insurance Law apply to my offence` IS
    `s 21A(2) the provisions of s 326(g) of the Insurance Law apply` `the offence is a security terror offence as s 326(g) of the Insurance Law has it`

§§ `What can reduce, delay or stop my allowance, or cost me a fine? (ss 18, 19(b), 20B, 23(b))`

-- s 18. The Institute may reduce, suspend or revoke a benefit of one who broke vocational training or rehabilitation instructions, or acted in a way publicly known to prevent or delay recovery.
@export Can the Institute reduce, suspend or revoke my allowance (s 18)?
GIVEN `I broke, without sufficient justification, instructions given in connection with vocational training or vocational rehabilitation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you break, without sufficient justification, instructions given in connection with vocational training or vocational rehabilitation?
      `I acted in a way publicly known to be liable to prevent or delay recovery or the return of my capacity to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you act in a way publicly known to be liable to prevent or delay your recovery, or the return of your capacity to work?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Institute reduce, suspend or revoke my allowance` IS
    `s 18 the Institute may reduce, suspend or revoke the benefit`
        `I broke, without sufficient justification, instructions given in connection with vocational training or vocational rehabilitation`
        `I acted in a way publicly known to be liable to prevent or delay recovery or the return of my capacity to work`

-- s 19(b). If the claimant or recipient does not meet a s 19(a) demand, the Institute may delay the claim, stop payment or refuse the benefit.
@export Can the Institute delay my claim or stop my allowance because I did not meet its demand (s 19(b))?
GIVEN `the Institute made a demand under s 19(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Institute make a demand of you under s 19(a) (information, an examination or an appearance)?
      `I have not met the demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not met the demand?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Institute delay my claim or stop my allowance because I did not meet its demand` IS
    `s 19(b) the Institute may delay the claim, stop payment or refuse the benefit`
        `the Institute made a demand under s 19(a)`
        `I have not met the demand`

-- s 23(b). A benefit cannot be transferred, pledged or attached in any way, not even to pay maintenance the recipient owes under a judgment.
@export Can my allowance be transferred, pledged or attached (s 23(b))?
GIVEN `the act is a transfer, a pledge or an attachment of my allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a transfer, a pledge or an attachment of the allowance, for any purpose, including paying maintenance you owe under a judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my allowance be transferred, pledged or attached` IS
    `s 23(b) the benefit may be transferred, pledged or attached` `the act is a transfer, a pledge or an attachment of my allowance`

-- s 20B(a). A claimant who made a false declaration about, or concealed, information the Institute needs to decide entitlement, rate or updating is liable to a fine.
@export Am I liable to a fine for a false declaration or concealment (s 20B(a))?
GIVEN `I made a false declaration about information the Institute needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a false declaration about information the Institute needs to determine entitlement to a benefit, its rate or its updating?
      `I concealed such information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you conceal such information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to a fine for a false declaration or concealment` IS
    `s 20B(a) the claimant is liable to a fine`
        `I made a false declaration about information the Institute needs`
        `I concealed such information`

-- s 20B(b)(1). A recipient who got a registered notice about the Fifth Schedule details, and did not report a change in time, is liable to a fine.
@export Am I liable to a fine for not reporting a change after a registered notice (s 20B(b)(1))?
GIVEN `I got a registered notice about the details in the Fifth Schedule that I must report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you get a registered notice about the details in the Fifth Schedule that affect entitlement or rate and that you must report?
      `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice sent?
      `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the change in one of those details happen?
      `I reported the change in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you report the change in writing?
      `the day I reported the change` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you report it? (Ignored if you have not.)
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to a fine for not reporting a change after a registered notice` IS
    `s 20B(b)(1) the recipient is liable to a fine`
        `I got a registered notice about the details in the Fifth Schedule that I must report`
        `the day the notice was sent`
        `the day of the change`
        (IF `I reported the change in writing` THEN JUST `the day I reported the change` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day I am asking about`

@export Does the notice I got meet the content requirements (s 20B(b)(2))?
GIVEN `the notice carries the warning in the words of part C of the Fifth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice carry the warning in the words of part C of the Fifth Schedule?
      `the notice is in Hebrew, Arabic, Russian and Amharic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in Hebrew, Arabic, Russian and Amharic?
      `the percentages of the basic amount are also shown in new shekels` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the percentages of the basic amount also shown in new shekels?
      `a form for updating the details in Hebrew is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a form for updating the details, in Hebrew, attached?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice I got meet the content requirements` IS
    `s 20B(b)(2) the notice meets the content requirements`
        `the notice carries the warning in the words of part C of the Fifth Schedule`
        `the notice is in Hebrew, Arabic, Russian and Amharic`
        `the percentages of the basic amount are also shown in new shekels`
        `a form for updating the details in Hebrew is attached`

@export Is the registered notice treated as delivered to me (s 20B(b)(3))?
GIVEN `the notice was sent by registered mail to the address I last gave the Institute and to the address in the population registry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent by registered mail to the address you last gave the Institute and to the address in the population registry?
      `the day the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice sent?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `I prove that I did not receive it for reasons beyond my control and not by avoiding it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove you did not receive the notice, for reasons beyond your control and not by avoiding it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the registered notice treated as delivered to me` IS
    `s 20B(b)(3) the notice is deemed served`
        `the notice was sent by registered mail to the address I last gave the Institute and to the address in the population registry`
        `the day the notice was sent`
        `the day I am asking about`
        `I prove that I did not receive it for reasons beyond my control and not by avoiding it`

@export Am I fined all the same if I did not receive the notice (s 20B(b)(4))?
GIVEN `I prove I did not receive the registered notice for reasons beyond my control and not by avoiding it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove you did not receive the registered notice, for reasons beyond your control and not by avoiding it?
      `I received the notice from an employee of the Institute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the notice from an employee of the Institute?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I fined all the same if I did not receive the notice` IS
    `s 20B(b)(4) paragraph (1) applies to the recipient all the same`
        `I prove I did not receive the registered notice for reasons beyond my control and not by avoiding it`
        `I received the notice from an employee of the Institute`

@export Am I excused from the fine because of a disability or a need for supervision (s 20B(b)(5))?
GIVEN `a medical disability was determined for me under item 33, 34 or 91 of the list of impairments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a medical disability determined for you under item 33, 34 or 91 of the list of impairments?
      `I was found to need constant supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found to need constant supervision, as s 224(a)(2) of the Insurance Law has it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I excused from the fine because of a disability or a need for supervision` IS
    `s 20B(b)(5) subsection (b) does not apply to the recipient`
        `a medical disability was determined for me under item 33, 34 or 91 of the list of impairments`
        `I was found to need constant supervision`

§§ `What can I be made to repay? (ss 17, 20A, 23(a))`

-- The Law has no section of its own on repaying an overpaid benefit.  Section 20A makes s 327 of the Insurance Law apply to one who claims or receives a benefit, and
-- s 23(a) lists the Insurance Law sections that apply to this Law.  Neither section is in the sources, so the answer is NOTHING where the question reaches into the Insurance Law.
@export Does s 327 of the National Insurance Law apply to me (s 20A)?
GIVEN `I claim or receive a benefit or a grant under this Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim or receive a benefit or a grant under this Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 327 of the National Insurance Law apply to me` IS
    `s 20A the provisions of s 327 of the Insurance Law apply to the person` `I claim or receive a benefit or a grant under this Law`

@export Does this section of the National Insurance Law apply to the allowance (s 23(a))?
GIVEN `the section number, as written in the Insurance Law` IS A STRING @desc Which section of the National Insurance Law are you asking about? (Write the number, for example 303.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this section of the National Insurance Law apply to the allowance` IS
    `s 23(a) the section of the Insurance Law applies to this Law` `the section number, as written in the Insurance Law`

@export Can the Institute claim compensation from me because I owe maintenance to someone it paid (s 17(a))?
GIVEN `I am liable by law or by agreement for the maintenance of someone who was paid a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable, by law or by agreement, for the maintenance of someone who was paid a benefit under this Law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Institute claim compensation from me because I owe maintenance to someone it paid` IS
    `s 17(a) the Institute may claim compensation from the person` `I am liable by law or by agreement for the maintenance of someone who was paid a benefit`

§§ `Which court hears my case? (ss 17(c), 26)`

@export May the District Court hear the Institute's compensation claim (s 17(c))?
GIVEN `the claim is the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the District Court hear the Institute's compensation claim` IS
    `s 17(c) the District Court may hear the claim` `the claim is the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17`

@export May a religious court also hear the Institute's compensation claim (s 17(c))?
GIVEN `the claim is the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17?
      `a religious court is hearing the maintenance rights of the person who was paid the benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a religious court hearing the maintenance rights of the person who was paid the benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a religious court also hear the Institute's compensation claim` IS
    `s 17(c) the religious court may also hear the claim`
        `the claim is the Institute's claim for compensation under s 17`
        `a religious court is hearing the maintenance rights of the person who was paid the benefit`

@export Does the Regional Labour Court have exclusive jurisdiction over my case (s 26)?
GIVEN `the action is under this Law or arises from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought under this Law, or does it arise from it?
      `the action is a claim under s 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a claim under s 17 (the Institute's claim for compensation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Regional Labour Court have exclusive jurisdiction over my case` IS
    `s 26 the Regional Labour Court has exclusive jurisdiction`
        `the action is under this Law or arises from it`
        `the action is a claim under s 17`

§§ `Who pays, and when the body is at fault (ss 14(c)(2), 22, 25)`

@export Who pays my allowance (s 25(a))?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Who pays my allowance` IS
    `s 25(a) who pays the benefit`

-- s 14(c)(2). One paid for a period before the month of claim under s 14(c)(1) has the privileges that a law, or a public body by agreement or custom, gives to one paid a benefit for that period.
@export Does being paid for a period before my claim give me the privileges others paid for such a period get (s 14(c)(2))?
GIVEN `I am paid the benefit under s 14(c)(1) for a period before the month of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid the benefit under s 14(c)(1) for a period before the month of your claim?
      `a law, or a public body under an agreement or custom, gives the privilege to one paid a benefit for that earlier period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a law, or a public body under an agreement or custom, give the privilege to people paid a benefit for an earlier period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does being paid for a period before my claim give me the privileges others paid for such a period get` IS
    `s 14(c)(2) the person paid under paragraph (1) is entitled to the privilege`
        `I am paid the benefit under s 14(c)(1) for a period before the month of the claim`
        `a law, or a public body under an agreement or custom, gives the privilege to one paid a benefit for that earlier period`

-- s 22. A member of the administration, a manager or an officer of a body is treated as responsible for the body's offence unless they prove it was without their knowledge or that they took every suitable measure.
@export Am I treated as responsible for my body's offence (s 22)?
GIVEN `the body I manage committed an offence by not doing what this Law or its regulations require of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the body commit an offence by not doing what this Law or its regulations require of it?
      `I am a member of the body's administration, a manager or an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the body's administration, a manager or an officer?
      `I prove that the offence was committed without my knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that the offence was committed without your knowledge?
      `I prove that I took every suitable measure to prevent the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you took every suitable measure to prevent the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as responsible for my body's offence` IS
    `s 22 the manager is treated as responsible for the body's offence`
        `the body I manage committed an offence by not doing what this Law or its regulations require of it`
        `I am a member of the body's administration, a manager or an officer`
        `I prove that the offence was committed without my knowledge`
        `I prove that I took every suitable measure to prevent the offence`
